{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game balance game balance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md","fileName":"Game Balance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Balance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Balance and Progression]] · [[Game Balance and Difficulty]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Balance and Progression","Game Balance and Difficulty","Game-Player System","Playtesting","Play Space","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game balance game balance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md","fileName":"Game Balance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Balance","heading":"Game Balance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Game balance is a dynamically stable relationship among parts, systems, progression, and players. A balanced game avoids an inherent or insurmountable advantage, preserves several viable strategies, and lets players recover from reasonable risks.\n\nBalance is a property of the whole [[Game-Player System]], not only of numeric equality between parts. It combines designer judgment, [[Playtesting]], player analytics, and mathematical models while keeping the [[Play Space]] perturbable and meaningful.\n\nThe source distinguishes competitive balance from player-versus-environment difficulty management. A balanced competitive game avoids dominant strategies and preserves the relevance of skill despite chance; a balanced environmental game keeps perceived difficulty within a credible range as challenge, player power, and experience change.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Balance and Progression","Game Balance and Difficulty","Game-Player System","Playtesting","Play Space","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game balance game balance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Balance.md","fileName":"Game Balance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Balance","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Balance and Progression","Game Balance and Difficulty","Game-Player System","Playtesting","Play Space","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}